  "reading_notes": {
    "margin_is_not_the_limiter": "the blend weight on the correction is 0.5105 at margin 0.06863 and 0.5096 at margin 0.01999: a 3.4x change of the store's read margin moves the blend by less than 0.002, so the failure is not a margin shortfall",
    "why_half_half": "the correction and the old entry share one address: their keys differ only by word order, cos = nearest_cos in correction_direction_band (~0.96), and the cosine softmax at temperature 0.1 turns that same-address gap into a near tie; the read value is 0.51 * v' + 0.49 * v_old, residual 0.698 = 0.49 * sqrt(2)",
    "value_at_1_is_a_tie_break": "value_at_1 is 1.0 on both rungs only because 0.511 > 0.489; it must not be read as 'the corrected value was returned'. The honest measure is the residual",
    "address_contract": "taiji/living_core.py addressed_write always takes a free slot and only evicts the oldest when the store is full; a near-identical key never supersedes the entry it duplicates, so a correction accumulates instead of replacing",
    "in_place_overwrite": "the overwrite diagnostic writes v' into the existing slot and reads clean (correction@1 = 1.0, top-1 is the rule entry) at both rungs: the geometry is sufficient, what is missing is a supersede rule, not more capacity",
    "legacy_encoder": "mean pooling is blind to word order, so the correction key is an exact copy (overlap 1.0, separation 0.0) and its softmax weight is the uniform share 1/(N+1): 0.113 at 9 entries, 0.016 at 65 entries"
  },
  "decision": "fail_geometry_holds_but_unreadable|geometry_holds_but_unreadable",
  "what_this_means": "correction@1 is the fraction of re-worded questions that retrieve the slot the correction was written to; value@1 is the fraction whose read value is closer to the corrected value than to the old one. They are reported apart because a content-addressed store can return the right slot and still hand back a blend of old and new when two entries share one address",
  "what_this_does_not_mean": [
    "no training, no optimizer step and no model forward ran; nothing here says the correction survives training",
    "the fixture is synthetic: a minority of real corrections are re-wordings of the same question, this probe measures exactly that case and nothing else",
    "value payloads are random unit vectors in the 20.3a payload shape; the readout is a cosine test, not a language-level judgement of the corrected answer",
    "the overlap/band reading is a geometric verdict on one key, not a calibrated threshold for real stores",
    "one session, one seed, no persistence across checkpoints"
  ],
